@1-14
The config and highlight modules plus imports: eframe/egui widgets, the bezier shape for the link strip, the native file dialog, filesystem access and PathBuf.

@15-48
The binding palette. Each link index gets a slightly different cool shade; the same shade is used for the pane tint, the band and the curves. Selection brightens the colour and thickens the stroke.

@50-84
The option tables used by the Settings menu: dark/light themes, six accent colour schemes, the language list (auto plus fourteen languages) and three syntax palettes.

@86-131
scheme_accent maps a colour-scheme name to an accent for the current theme, with a darker accent in light mode so it stays readable.

@133-149
apply_theme rebuilds egui visuals from dark or light defaults, then overrides the selection, hyperlink, hover/active fills and widget strokes with the chosen accent. It runs once per frame before the panels.

@151-166
All app state in one struct: source and comment text, both paths, status line, parsed blocks, selected link, scroll offsets, the one-frame scroll source flag, and the TOML settings.

@168-239
paint_pane draws one pane below its TextEdit: background, one rounded and padded coloured band per linked block, a gutter, and line numbers for the visible lines when the setting is on. On the comment side the band stops before trailing blank lines, so the empty lines between sections stay untinted and clearly separate the blocks while the gutter keeps counting them. Each pane may use a different font and row height.

@241-322
paint_links draws two cubic bezier curves per block in the 44 pixel middle strip, one for the first line and one for the last line. Each curve ends in a small filled triangle that points into the pane like a comic speech balloon tail. A faint inset band between the curves shows the whole range, and selection brightens and thickens everything. The two panes can have different row heights.

@324-370
open reads a source file, derives the .cmt path beside it, reads or starts an empty comment file, normalizes the section spacing, and remembers the source path. save writes only the comment file. refresh reparses blocks and drops a selection that no longer exists.

@371-443
Settings persistence and helpers: remember_last_file writes the current source path into config.toml; save_settings writes the whole config; set_space_lines re-normalizes the comment file; set_source_font and set_comment_font clamp the font sizes; active_language resolves the auto-detected or overridden language; select_relative wraps through the links.

@444-453
open_target is the platform shim used by the Help and Settings menus for URLs and for the config file path: cmd /C start on Windows, open on macOS, xdg-open elsewhere.

@455-461
The update loop applies the theme, then still handles Ctrl+S by saving the comment pane.

@463-680
A classic top menu in a TopBottomPanel, built with egui::menu::bar and menu_button like ct. File opens/saves/exits; View moves between links and resets scroll; Settings toggles preferences and exposes theme, accent colours, syntax highlighting, language, highlight palette, space lines and both font sizes; Help opens the project page and shows About.

@681-684
The status line lives in a bottom TopBottomPanel, so the central panel is reserved for the two panes.

@685-756
Layout maths: two equal panes, a 44 pixel link strip with room for the bezier tails, 6 pixel gaps, and a gutter inside each pane that is sized from the widest line number plus a small pad. Scroll handoff maps the centre of one pane through the linked ranges into the other using each pane's own row height.

@757-795
Both panes and the link strip are painted before the text widgets are added, so the bands stay behind the text. The source pane is read-only but selectable; the comment pane is editable.

@796-866
Two ScrollAreas use their own font and row height. Each pane lives in a child UI with a distinct id source ("source_pane" / "comment_pane"), so egui does not report duplicate widget ids, and each child is clipped to its own text rect so long lines cannot bleed into the other pane. The editor is added left-aligned rather than with add_sized, which would centre oversized text and push it left over the source pane. The source editor always uses a layouter: it runs the highlighter when highlighting is enabled, otherwise it builds plain text. The comment editor uses a simple no-wrap layouter and shows the marker-free view of the .cmt file. Neither pane wraps, so every galley row stays on its physical line.

@868-913
Click selection: a click on a source line, a comment line or a curve sets the selected block, using the row height of that pane. Clicking the strip picks the nearest curve by vertical distance.

@914-925
Scroll detection compares the new offsets with the previous frame. applied_sync suppresses the echo from a scroll we caused ourselves.

@926-933
Any edit to the visible comment text is mapped back into the canonical file with restore_markers, then triggers a reparse so new markers and changed ranges appear in the same frame.

@934-961
Entry point. The window is 1100 by 760; settings are loaded first, then a command-line path is opened, otherwise the remembered last file if that setting is enabled.

@963-967
Gutter width helper: the digit count comes from the line total, the digit width from the active monospace font, and the result adds 4 pixels of left pad and 6 pixels of breathing room before the text, never below 18.
